## What a Wedding Actually Needs, and Where MEG Fits

A wedding rental list usually breaks into a handful of trades: seating, tables and linens from a furniture or event rental company, catering contracted through the venue or a caterer, decor and florals from a florist or stylist, photography and video as their own trade, and audio visual, sound, lighting, microphones and technical support, as the last category. That last one is the trade MEG's own inventory covers. If the venue and your other vendors still leave a gap, a missing table or a tent for the terrace, tell us what it is. We can check which of our suppliers, if any, has one free on your date, and we will be clear with you that it is sourced.

A provider bundling everything into one marketing package is usually still subcontracting most of it to other trades. The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) bundles only its own AV slice into one price rather than four separate rentals. See our [all in one wedding rental packages](/blog/all-in-one-wedding-rental-packages/) guide for exactly what that does and does not include, and our [questions to ask a wedding rental company](/blog/questions-to-ask-wedding-rental-companies/) guide for how to get an honest, itemized breakdown from any provider you're comparing.

