## A Malaga Detail: What Fincas and Villas Often Include

One thing a generic checklist misses, and something absent from the US based guides that dominate this search, is how differently Costa del Sol venues package their own hire. Many fincas and villas around Malaga bundle a base level of furniture, chairs, tables, sometimes basic linens, into the venue rental itself, rather than leaving a couple to source it separately. This is general market context, not a claim about any specific venue, so confirm what your venue already includes before renting furniture on top of it.

What is rarely bundled in is professional AV: a PA system sized for the guest count, ambient lighting beyond the venue's own fixtures, wireless microphones for vows and speeches, and a technician who stays for the event. That is where the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) fits, regardless of what your venue provides on the furniture side. If your reception is outdoors, a common setup at fincas and villas around Malaga, see our [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guide for the power, curfew and placement questions that come with it. For an indoor reception, see our [indoor wedding rental essentials](/blog/indoor-wedding-rental-essentials/) guide for how room acoustics and accent lighting change the setup instead.

## Getting Ceremony and Reception Sound Right

Two audio decisions come up in nearly every wedding we set up.

### Wired or Wireless Microphone for Vows

For the ceremony itself, the standard setup is a wireless handheld microphone from the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/), which includes professional wireless microphones for speeches and announcements. The officiant holds it, there is no cable across the aisle, and our technician on site watches the levels through the vows. The same wireless handhelds then carry the speeches and toasts at the reception, where guests move between the microphone and their seats and a cable would get in the way. If the officiant prefers a wired handheld, we own wired dynamic microphones and one can be an alternative on request. If hands free matters more, we also stock a wireless lavalier microphone as a separate add on: see our [headset and lavalier microphone rental](/blog/headset-lavalier-microphone-rental/) guide for the full comparison and pricing. Tell us when you book if your ceremony calls for either, so we bring the right setup.

### Ceremony Sound Is a Different Job Than Reception Sound

Ceremony sound is about intelligibility for a seated, listening audience during vows and readings, so the PA is tuned for clarity at a lower volume. Reception sound has to cover speeches at similar clarity, then switch to music at dance volume in the same room, a different tuning task entirely. A technician who stays on site for both, rather than a single drop off delivery, adjusts the system as the day moves from ceremony to speeches to dancing. For the deeper ceremony specific detail, lapel versus handheld mic choice and how wind and waves change speaker placement, see our [unique wedding ceremony rentals](/blog/unique-wedding-ceremony-rentals/) guide.

