## FAQs

### What items does Malaga Event Gear actually provide for a wedding?

PA sound, ambient lighting, wireless microphones and a live technician, bundled in the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) for 650 euros ex VAT. Furniture, tents, linens and decor are not in our own inventory, and catering is not a service we run. See [What a Wedding Actually Needs, and Where MEG Fits](#what-a-wedding-actually-needs-and-where-meg-fits) above.

### Does the Wedding Pack include chairs, tables or linens?

No. Those come from a furniture rental company or, in many cases, are already included in the venue's own hire.

### Do venues around Malaga usually include furniture in the hire?

Many fincas and villas on the Costa del Sol bundle a base level of furniture into the venue rental itself. This varies by venue, so confirm directly with yours before renting furniture separately.

### Should ceremony microphones be wired or wireless?

Wireless is the standard. The Wedding Pack's wireless handheld microphones cover the officiant during the vows and the guests during the reception speeches and toasts, with our technician watching levels throughout. A wired handheld can be an alternative on request, and a wireless lavalier is a separate item if the officiant needs both hands free. See [Wired or Wireless Microphone for Vows](#wired-or-wireless-microphone-for-vows) above.

### Is ceremony sound the same setup as reception sound?

No. Ceremony sound is tuned for clarity at a lower volume for a seated audience. Reception sound covers speeches at similar clarity, then switches to music at dance volume, a different tuning task our live technician adjusts for throughout the event.
